```
This will create a link with the text "Read More" and a dynamic `href` attribute that will be generated using the `post_id`.

2. Modify the Nginx configuration to include the new HTML file as the index file for the `/` location:
```diff
location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index post-link.html index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /post-link.html;
}
```
This will serve the `post-link.html` file as the index page when a user visits the root URL (`/`) of your website.

3. Update the Nginx configuration to include the `post_id` in the URL:
```diff
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.askfundu.com;
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;

    # ...

    map $uri $post_id {
        ~^/post/(\d+) $1;
    }

    # ...
}
```
This will define a new Nginx variable `post_id` that extracts the `post_id` from the URL using a regular expression.

4. Update the `location /` block to include the `post_id` in the HTML link:
```diff
location / {
    root /usr/share/nginx/html;
    index post-link.html index.html index.htm;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /post-link.html;

    set $post_id $matches[1];

    <a href="/post/{{$post_id}}" class="post-link">Read More</a>
}
```
This will set the `post_id` variable and include it in the HTML link.

5. Create a new Nginx location block to handle the `post` route:
```diff
